{
  "name": "What to Do When Your Home Needs a Wheelchair Ramp",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you've realized a wheelchair ramp is becoming a necessity for your home – that's a big step towards improving accessibility! But what's next? First off, you'll want to measure the vertical rise. This is super important because it directly impacts how long your ramp needs to be to maintain a safe and usable slope. A common guide is to have at least one foot of ramp for every inch of height. Next, think about where the ramp will go and if you have enough space for it, including a flat landing area at the top and bottom. Don't forget to check your doorway width to ensure there’s enough clearance. There are different ramp types and materials, from modular aluminum to custom-built wood, each with pros and cons in terms of durability, maintenance, and cost. Many places also require permits for permanent ramps, so checking with your local authorities early can save you headaches. Getting an in-home evaluation from a pro, like us at HH Remodeling LLC, can really help iron out all these details and make sure you're getting a safe, code-compliant, and perfectly fitted ramp.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
